{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBy3pn5iJXS6vk2YFuLU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The O3 frontend formats dates in one shared utility in `openmrs-esm-core`, and the \"Today\" label comes from the browser's `Intl.RelativeTimeFormat`, not from a translation string.\n\n**How it works**\n\n1. **Locale source.** `getLocale()` reads `window.i18next.language`, normalizes it to a BCP 47 tag, and maps `ht` to `fr-HT` (`openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/get-locale.ts:7-18`).\n2. **Entry point.** `formatDate(date, options)` resolves the locale and merges options over defaults: `mode: 'standard'`, `time: 'for today'`, `day`/`month`/`year: true`, and `noToday: false`. It sets `noToday: true` automatically for `am` (Amharic) (`openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts:306-314`).\n3. **\"Today\" branch.** If `dayjs(date).isToday()` is true and `noToday` is false, it calls `new Intl.RelativeTimeFormat(locale, { numeric: 'auto' }).format(0, 'day')`. That yields \"today\" in the locale's language, and the first letter is uppercased (`date-util.ts:326-332`).\n4. **Other dates.** Otherwise it uses `Intl.DateTimeFormat` with `year`, `month: 'short'`, and `day: '2-digit'`. For `en` it switches the locale to `en-GB` so AM/PM is shown for times. For `en`/`am` in standard mode it joins parts with hyphens, and `wide` mode uses ` — ` as the separator (`date-util.ts:333-366`).\n5. **Time.** The time is appended as `, ${formatTime(date)}` when `time === true`, or when the date is today and `time` is `'for today'`. `formatTime` uses `toLocaleTimeString(getLocale(), { hour: '2-digit', minute: '2-digit' })` (`date-util.ts:368-401`).\n6. **Variants.** `formatDatetime` forces `time: true` (`date-util.ts:416-418`). `formatPartialDate` parses partial strings such as \"2000-01\" and then calls `formatDate` (`date-util.ts:241-280`).\n\n**Documentation**\n\n- The generated function page `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/formatDate.md` states the defaults and says \"Today\" is produced in the locale language, with `noToday: true` to disable it.\n- `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/type-aliases/FormatDateOptions.md` documents `noToday` as the switch between \"Today\" and the normal format (line 69).\n- The source JSDoc on `FormatDateOptions` and `formatDate` (`date-util.ts:172-206`, `date-util.ts:282-304`) carries the same description.\n\nI did not find a separate date helper in `openmrs-esm-patient-chart`; the chart uses these helpers from the framework. I also did not read the `formatPartialDate.md` docs page, though a search hit shows it has the same \"Today\" note.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts\", \"startLine\": 306, \"endLine\": 372},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts\", \"startLine\": 282, \"endLine\": 304},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts\", \"startLine\": 416, \"endLine\": 418},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts\", \"startLine\": 396, \"endLine\": 401},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts\", \"startLine\": 241, \"endLine\": 280},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts\", \"startLine\": 172, \"endLine\": 215},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts\", \"startLine\": 164, \"endLine\": 168},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts\", \"startLine\": 64, \"endLine\": 66},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/get-locale.ts\", \"startLine\": 7, \"endLine\": 18},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/formatDate.md\", \